WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:10.640 --> 00:00:12.600
Good morning, John; it's Tuesday, July 3rd.

00:00:12.600 --> 00:00:15.000
How long am I gonna be on the odd days?

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:16.680
I'm tired of the odd days.

00:00:16.680 --> 00:00:18.560
Out on the porch again on a porch swing.

00:00:18.560 --> 00:00:24.000
So if I look like I'm constantly moving to you it's because I'm constantly moving.

00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:25.840
Hopefully that's not going to make anybody nauseous.

00:00:25.840 --> 00:00:28.280
In reference to your new nerdfighter scheme,

00:00:28.280 --> 00:00:33.160
I am just mostly very happy 
at the abilities of our current nerdfighters.

00:00:33.160 --> 00:00:34.720
Because, damn!

00:00:34.720 --> 00:00:37.540
I couldn't actually keep up with the
amazingness of the nerdfighters.

00:00:37.540 --> 00:00:40.120
I went and had Brotherhood 2.0
sponsor a new person at kiva.org

00:00:40.120 --> 00:00:46.420
and then, by the time I was done,
and had gone away to, you know, urinate

00:00:46.420 --> 00:00:49.540
or something, I would come back
and it was already all the way funded.

00:00:49.540 --> 00:00:52.200
People are really excited about this idea.

00:00:52.200 --> 00:00:54.520
Which, I think that they should be.

00:00:54.520 --> 00:00:57.740
However, you're right, there
could be more nerdfighters.

00:00:57.740 --> 00:00:59.600
and more nerdfighters
would be a good thing.

00:00:59.620 --> 00:01:02.240
I'm excited for all you new
senior executive nerdfighters.

00:01:02.240 --> 00:01:04.620
I'm sure we will have
projects for you soon.

00:01:04.620 --> 00:01:07.740
And don't worry. If you've seen more than
one episode of Brotherhood 2.0

00:01:07.740 --> 00:01:09.640
you're not really a nit anymore.

00:01:09.640 --> 00:01:10.880
You're a nerdfighter.

00:01:10.880 --> 00:01:13.740
We'd love it if you'd comment more,
and I'd like to see you in my pants.

00:01:13.740 --> 00:01:15.260
And rating our videos on YouTube

00:01:15.260 --> 00:01:17.640
Getting "nerdfighter" tattooed across your face

00:01:17.640 --> 00:01:21.360
Actually I seem to remember a point
in time where people were sending us

00:01:21.360 --> 00:01:24.420
cool little nerdfighter things
that they were doing

00:01:24.420 --> 00:01:28.340
like one person spelled "NERD FITR"
on their knuckles and sent us a picture

00:01:28.340 --> 00:01:31.580
one person made an Easter egg that
said "nerdfighters" on it

00:01:31.580 --> 00:01:33.900
I would like to encourage people to do that more.

00:01:33.900 --> 00:01:36.580
Those made really good middle
frames for the YouTube clip.

00:01:36.580 --> 00:01:39.580
Someone said they did sidewalk chalk
nerdfighters in their driveway.

00:01:39.580 --> 00:01:41.320
Advertise yourself as a nerdfighter.

00:01:41.320 --> 00:01:43.720
Do nerdfighter stuff,

00:01:43.720 --> 00:01:46.520
uh, mostly just with
the word "nerdfighter",

00:01:46.520 --> 00:01:51.160
and send it to us, and it's extremely
likely that it will be on the show.

00:01:51.160 --> 00:01:54.320
I do have one other little bit
of business to attend to.

00:01:54.320 --> 00:01:56.600
You do know what a Decepticon is, right?

00:01:56.600 --> 00:01:58.600
You know, you didn't
make up that word.

00:01:58.600 --> 00:02:01.160
Decepticons are Transformers,
the enemies of the Autobots.

00:02:01.900 --> 00:02:06.140
When you chose Decepticons as
a name for a nerdfighter's enemy,

00:02:06.140 --> 00:02:09.620
I initially thought that there must be
some better team of supervillains

00:02:09.620 --> 00:02:10.900
to use as our enemies.

00:02:10.900 --> 00:02:14.360
Then I looked, and I realized that
supervillains don't come in teams,

00:02:14.360 --> 00:02:19.060
supervillains almost always work alone
with henchmen below them.

00:02:19.060 --> 00:02:22.360
And the Decepticons are kind of a
gigantic exception to that rule.

00:02:22.360 --> 00:02:25.580
I kept thinking of different villains
from cartoons from my childhood

00:02:25.580 --> 00:02:29.620
Dr. Claw, Shredder, Mumm-Ra, Skeletor

00:02:29.620 --> 00:02:31.300
you know, people like that.

00:02:31.300 --> 00:02:33.440
But the Decepticons really are
a team of supervillains,

00:02:33.440 --> 00:02:34.540
and I think that's impressive.

00:02:34.540 --> 00:02:38.740
And frankly, as the enemy of
nerdfighters do operate in teams

00:02:38.740 --> 00:02:40.400
they're not on their own.

00:02:40.400 --> 00:02:41.640
They don't have henchmen.

00:02:41.640 --> 00:02:46.240
I think Decepticons is, so far,
a pretty good name for them.

00:02:46.240 --> 00:02:49.100
Anyhow, I will see you tommorow.

